# Story: As a security officer, I want repeated failed sign-ins to lock an account for a while, so that passwords cannot be guessed by trying many of them. After five failed sign-ins for one username within fifteen minutes, sign-in for that username is refused for five minutes with TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS, even with the right password. Other accounts are not affected.

@draft
Feature: Account Lockout After Multiple Failed Sign-Ins

  Scenario Outline: Account gets locked after five failed sign-in attempts within fifteen minutes
    Given a user has attempted to sign in with an incorrect password four times for the same username within fifteen minutes
    When they attempt to sign in again with the correct password
    Then their sign-in is refused because "TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS"
    
    Examples:
      | username |
      | alice    |

  Scenario Outline: Account can be used after five minute lockout period ends
    Given a user has attempted to sign in with an incorrect password four times for the same username within fifteen minutes
    And their sign-in is refused because "TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS"
    When they wait for five minutes and attempt to sign in again with the correct password
    Then their sign-in is successful

    Examples:
      | username |
      | alice    |

  Scenario Outline: Other accounts are not affected by failed attempts on one account
    Given a user has attempted to sign in with an incorrect password four times for the same username within fifteen minutes
    And another user tries to sign in with their correct credentials immediately after
    Then the other user's sign-in is successful

    Examples:
      | username |
      | alice    |
      | bob      |

  Scenario Outline: Sign-in attempts are counted over a sliding window of fifteen minutes
    Given a user has attempted to sign in with an incorrect password four times for the same username within fifteen minutes
    And they wait more than fifteen minutes and attempt to sign in again with the correct password
    Then their sign-in is successful

    Examples:
      | username |
      | alice    |

  Scenario Outline: Sign-in attempts are counted correctly even if there's a mix of failed and successful attempts
    Given a user has attempted to sign in with an incorrect password three times for the same username within fifteen minutes
    And they attempt to sign in successfully once
    When they attempt to sign in again with an incorrect password twice more within fifteen minutes
    Then their sign-in is refused because "TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS"

    Examples:
      | username |
      | alice    |
